            <ArticleTitle>Factors predicting coronary artery disease in patients with giant negative T waves.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>873-5, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Seventy-four patients with giant negative T waves were studied to determine which electrocardiographic variables predicted the presence of coronary artery disease. The absence of left ventricular hypertrophy and the presence of symmetric T-wave inversion predicted coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
